Checkpoint 13 - quiet 30-minute full-system baseline
====================================================

Purpose
-------

Establish a no-failure baseline before recovery code or crash injection. The
target starts the three full-scope containerized ingestion workers immediately.
Ten minutes later it starts exactly one sequential workflow:

1. Windy discovery;
2. Fintraffic discovery;
3. Skaping discovery;
4. verified PostgreSQL backup and conservative backup cleanup;
5. transformation-scoped cleanup of images older than 24 hours.

At thirty minutes the target stops only the three ingestion workers. Monitoring
and core infrastructure remain available. A workflow already in progress is
allowed to finish, so its actual duration and whether discovery fitted inside
the thirty-minute ingestion window remain observable.

Administrator installation
----------------------------

    sudo cp \
      /home/codexuser/src/webcam-iot-ingest/deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-30min-baseline/webcam-checkpoint13-baseline* \
      /etc/systemd/system/
    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemd-analyze verify \
      /etc/systemd/system/webcam-checkpoint13-baseline*.service \
      /etc/systemd/system/webcam-checkpoint13-baseline*.timer \
      /etc/systemd/system/webcam-checkpoint13-baseline.target

The `run-workflow` script remains in the repository and is invoked through its
absolute path; it must be executable.

Still from the administrator account, create a narrow sudo policy so
`codexuser` can control and inspect only this benchmark:

    sudo visudo -f /etc/sudoers.d/webcam-checkpoint13-baseline

Add the following content. Confirm the executable paths first with
`command -v systemctl journalctl`; replace `/usr/bin` below if this host uses a
different location.

    Cmnd_Alias WEBCAM_CP13_BASELINE = \
        /usr/bin/systemctl start webcam-checkpoint13-baseline.target, \
        /usr/bin/systemctl stop webcam-checkpoint13-baseline.target, \
        /usr/bin/systemctl --no-pager --full status webcam-checkpoint13-baseline*, \
        /usr/bin/journalctl -f -u webcam-checkpoint13-baseline*

    codexuser ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: WEBCAM_CP13_BASELINE

Then secure and validate the policy:

    sudo chown root:root /etc/sudoers.d/webcam-checkpoint13-baseline
    sudo chmod 0440 /etc/sudoers.d/webcam-checkpoint13-baseline
    sudo visudo -c

Do not grant unrestricted `systemctl`, `journalctl`, or root access.

Preflight as codexuser
----------------------

    cd /home/codexuser/src/webcam-iot-ingest
    docker compose --env-file .env --profile application \
      --profile monitoring --profile jobs config --quiet
    systemd-analyze verify \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-30min-baseline/*.service \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-30min-baseline/*.timer \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint13-30min-baseline/*.target
    docker compose ps
    sudo -n -l

Confirm that `sudo -n -l` lists `WEBCAM_CP13_BASELINE`. The `-n` option makes
an authorization error fail immediately instead of unexpectedly asking
`codexuser` for an administrator password.

Do not run another ingestion benchmark, discovery, backup, or cleanup command
in parallel with this baseline.

Start and observe
-----------------

    sudo -n systemctl start webcam-checkpoint13-baseline.target
    sudo -n systemctl --no-pager --full status \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline.target \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-stack.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-workflow.timer \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-stop.timer

    sudo -n journalctl -f \
      -u webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-workflow.service \
      -u 'webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-discovery@*.service' \
      -u webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-db-backup.service \
      -u webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-spool-cleanup.service

Worker logs remain container logs:

    docker compose logs -f --since 5m \
      windy-worker fintraffic-worker skaping-worker

Confirm all three workers are healthy:

    docker compose ps windy-worker fintraffic-worker skaping-worker

After thirty minutes
--------------------

    sudo -n systemctl --no-pager --full status \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline.target \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-workflow.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-discovery@windy.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-discovery@fintraffic.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-discovery@skaping.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-db-backup.service \
      webcam-checkpoint13-baseline-spool-cleanup.service

    docker compose ps windy-worker fintraffic-worker skaping-worker

Record worker throughput, latency, epoch duration, provider errors, PostgreSQL
connections, CPU, memory, disk, discovery durations, backup duration, cleanup
duration, and whether the workflow completed before or after the thirty-minute
deadline. Grafana and Prometheus remain running for inspection.

Stop early
----------

    sudo -n systemctl stop webcam-checkpoint13-baseline.target

Stopping early does not terminate a workflow that has already started. Stop an
individual workflow service explicitly only if necessary and from the
administrator account; the narrow `codexuser` policy deliberately does not
authorize that operation.
